      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nAcetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day. That is almost four times the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g/day. A single 5000 mg dose is also above the normal single dose of 500\u20131000 mg. At this level the risk of acute liver injury and liver failure is high, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** by mouth three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** by mouth every 6 hours (2.6 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** by mouth three times daily (3 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** by mouth four times daily (4 g/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you tell me the intended dose and frequency, I'll enter it right away. It's also worth checking the dose with your resident or pharmacist. If 5000 mg was intended, please have the supervising physician confirm it."
      }
     ],
